<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The brand mark, and the icon a fresh install gets: an open book with the
     bookmark ribbon in its gutter. Carried by the "crescent" activity-alias,
     which ships android:enabled="true", and reached first from
     Settings -> Interface.

     The background is the ink navy the artwork's own plate uses, so the two
     blend into one image instead of showing a ring around the mark.

     The foreground and monochrome layers are PNGs, not vectors as they were
     before: the mark carries a soft drop shadow, which a flat VectorDrawable
     cannot express, and one raster source guarantees the adaptive icon and the
     pre-26 legacy icon are pixel-identical. Generated by
     tool/gen_brand_assets.py — edit that, not these files.

     The artwork is fitted to the central 66dp of the 108dp canvas, so it
     survives the circular, squircle and rounded masks launchers apply. The
     monochrome layer is what Android 13+ tints to match the user's wallpaper;
     without it this would be the only icon on the homescreen that ignores the
     theme. It is a single colour by definition, so the red reads white there.

     The persisted icon id for this slot is "crescent", not "plain": ids are
     written into prefs on users' phones and cannot be renamed once shipped,
     whereas which mark an id carries is not frozen and has changed more than
     once. See AppIconService.defaultId. -->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@color/ic_launcher_bg" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_plain_fg" />
    <monochrome android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_plain_mono" />
</adaptive-icon>
